The conceptual ladder is: $\text{image}
\longrightarrow
\text{image-maker/thought}
\longrightarrow
\text{memory and concepts}
\longrightarrow
\text{psychological time}
\longrightarrow
\text{the known}.$ The arrow means the inquiry is led toward, not mechanical causation. Krishnamurti is not offering a theory of mind. He is showing why a merely verbal ending is insufficient.

