\neq
\text{universal sorrow}.$ Thought-made sorrow includes self-pity and the personal drama of the image. Universal sorrow is the deeper sorrow of mankind: ignorance, destruction, repeated wars, poverty, and the long continuity of human beings mistreating one another.

