p.src:
There is another puzzle. If universal sorrow ends, why does it still exist in mankind? The dialogue resolves this as a problem of language. In insight, sorrow ends for the one who sees; as a wider human fact, sorrow still goes on. Thus: $\text{insight into universal sorrow}
\longrightarrow
\text{sorrow ends in that seeing},$ while the disorder of mankind is not thereby magically erased as an external fact.

