p.src:
The tempting formula is: $\text{sorrow} \longrightarrow \text{compassion}.$ The dialogue corrects that formula. It would imply that one must go through sorrow first, as though suffering were a method. That implication is rejected. The more precise form is: $\text{ending of deeper sorrow}
\longrightarrow
\text{compassion}
\longrightarrow
\text{energy}.$ Even here the arrow must be read cautiously. It does not prescribe a technique. It records the way the discussion clarifies the relation.

